{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01DPYemut5EZtD9nzKG2ADgW","type":"tool_result","content":"26\t\n27\t/// The function-local `static int inner = 1;` of C's `static_alias()`.\n28\t///\n29\t/// A function-local static in C has static storage duration, i.e. exactly the\n30\t/// lifetime of the loaded image, and is shared by every call.\n31\tstatic mut INNER: c_int = 1;\n32\t\n33\t/// ```c\n34\t/// int*\n35\t/// static_alias(int *outer) {\n36\t///   static int inner = 1;\n37\t///   if(*outer >= inner) {\n38\t///     inner += *outer;\n39\t///     return &inner;\n40\t///   } else {\n41\t///     *outer += inner;\n42\t///     return outer;\n43\t///   }\n44\t/// }\n45\t/// ```\n46\t///\n47\t/// # Safety\n48\t/// `outer` must be a valid, aligned, dereferenceable and writable pointer to an\n49\t/// `int`, exactly as required by the C function.\n50\t#[no_mangle]\n51\tpub unsafe extern \"C\" fn static_alias(outer: *mut c_int) -> *mut c_int {\n52\t    let inner: *mut c_int = std::ptr::addr_of_mut!(INNER);\n53\t\n54\t    if *outer >= *inner {\n55\t        // `inner += *outer`; when `outer` aliases `inner` this doubles it.\n56\t        *inner = (*inner).wrapping_add(*outer);\n57\t        inner\n58\t    } else {\n59\t        *outer = (*outer).wrapping_add(*inner);\n60\t        outer\n61\t    }\n62\t}\n63\t\n64\t/// True for the characters `isspace()` accepts in the \"C\" locale, which is the\n65\t/// locale in effect because the program never calls `setlocale()`.\n66\tfn is_c_space(b: u8) -> bool {\n67\t    matches!(b, b' ' | b'\\t' | b'\\n' | 0x0b | 0x0c | b'\\r')\n68\t}\n69\t\n70\t/// Faithful replica of `strtol(s, &end, 10)`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de9cef2c-8983-4644-b640-090ad169eda3","uuid":"6d0c3dff-cf0c-4e49-b945-b28dc2e01e12","timestamp":"2026-08-18T00:07:47.970Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SuMYpu/translated_rust/src/lib.rs","content":"\n/// The function-local `static int inner = 1;` of C's `static_alias()`.\n///\n/// A function-local static in C has static storage duration, i.e. exactly the\n/// lifetime of the loaded image, and is shared by every call.\nstatic mut INNER: c_int = 1;\n\n/// ```c\n/// int*\n/// static_alias(int *outer) {\n///   static int inner = 1;\n///   if(*outer >= inner) {\n///     inner += *outer;\n///     return &inner;\n///   } else {\n///     *outer += inner;\n///     return outer;\n///   }\n/// }\n/// ```\n///\n/// # Safety\n/// `outer` must be a valid, aligned, dereferenceable and writable pointer to an\n/// `int`, exactly as required by the C function.\n#[no_mangle]\npub unsafe extern \"C\" fn static_alias(outer: *mut c_int) -> *mut c_int {\n    let inner: *mut c_int = std::ptr::addr_of_mut!(INNER);\n\n    if *outer >= *inner {\n        // `inner += *outer`; when `outer` aliases `inner` this doubles it.\n        *inner = (*inner).wrapping_add(*outer);\n        inner\n    } else {\n        *outer = (*outer).wrapping_add(*inner);\n        outer\n    }\n}\n\n/// True for the characters `isspace()` accepts in the \"C\" locale, which is the\n/// locale in effect because the program never calls `setlocale()`.\nfn is_c_space(b: u8) -> bool {\n    matches!(b, b' ' | b'\\t' | b'\\n' | 0x0b | 0x0c | b'\\r')\n}\n\n/// Faithful replica of `strtol(s, &end, 10)`.","numLines":45,"startLine":26,"totalLines":181}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ebcozvsqay4r4iqpbccc7hnbhmsakjobuwycfcfxjkmzlcpxhzmq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's what was done and found.\n\n## Setup\n\nThe project is a single-translation-unit C program (`c_src/src/main.c`: `static_alias` + `main`) that CMake builds as an **executable**, and `Cargo.toml` declared **no `[features]`** — so the feature cross-product is one (empty) combination, verified mechanically by `scripts/check_features.sh` (it derives the list from `Cargo.toml`, so it stays correct if features are added).\n\nTo make true FFI differential testing possible, the crate was restructured without changing its deliverable: logic moved to `src/lib.rs` (exports `#[no_mangle] static_alias`), `examples/capi.rs` is a cdylib exporting `#[no_mangle] main`, and `src/main.rs` remains the `driver` binary (it builds a real `argc`/`argv` and calls the translated `main`). Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (md5s unchanged; only the prescribed `build/` dir was added).\n\n## Phase A artifacts\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` defines exactly `main` + `static_alias`; both exported by the Rust `.so`. Symbol diff **empty** (re-derived with `nm -D` by `tests/symbols.rs`).\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 20 rows, all `[x]`: the 4 checks that actually exist in the C, plus `strtol` saturation, `long`→`int` narrowing, trailing garbage, empty/oversized strings, wild/negative `argc`, extra `argv`, `int` boundaries, and 4 NULL-pointer rows.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 30 rows, all `[x]`: both entry points, both branches, self-aliasing, hidden-static states (1/grown/0/negative/`INT_MIN`/wrapped), caller storage classes, argv shapes, iteration counts, repeated/interleaved calls, and process-environment axes.\n\n## Phases B–D\n28 tests / ~3.5k compared call pairs, every Rust call via `dlopen`+`dlsym` on the `.so` (stdout captured at fd level with `fflush(NULL)`; each scenario loads private `.so` copies so `static int inner` starts pristine). All green in **dev and release**, all feature combos, and against C built at `-O0/-O2/-O3`.\n\n**Two real divergences found and fixed:**\n1. **SIGPIPE**: `driver 1 20000000 | head -2` — C died with signal 13, Rust exited 0 (Rust's runtime sets `SIG_IGN`). Fixed in `src/main.rs`; regression test `cli_closed_pipe_sigpipe`.\n2. **Hidden static**: the original translation modelled aliasing with a bool + local variable — `static_alias` wasn't exported at all and state didn't survive across calls. Now a real `static mut INNER` with raw pointers, shared between `static_alias` and `main` as in C.\n\n**Test-suite validation:** `scripts/mutation_check.sh` injects 12 mutations (`>=`→`>`, wrapping→saturating in both branches, static's initial value, message text, removed parse check, removed saturation, loop off-by-one, `printf` format, `\\v` dropped, relaxed `argc`, clamped narrowing) → **12/12 detected**; `scripts/mutation_check_ffi.sh` → **8/8 detected by the dlopen-based tests alone**.\n\nOne documented caveat (in `ERRORS.md`): for `static_alias(NULL)` — UB in C — the dev profile's rustc UB checks abort (SIGABRT) where C segfaults; exact signal parity holds in release, and the dev-profile test asserts abnormal termination."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":996,"cache_read_input_tokens":254492,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":996,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de9cef2c-8983-4644-b640-090ad169eda3","uuid":"69015d65-9182-428c-b2c8-7eff76dc976f","timestamp":"2026-08-18T00:08:05.808Z"}
